ne":"Flash Flood Watch issued August 23 at 11:46AM MDT until August 23 at 9:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flash flooding and debris flows caused by excessive rainfall\ncontinue to be possible over the Aspen Acres burn scar.\n\n* WHERE...Aspen Acres Burn Scar.\n\n* WHEN...Until 9 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Heavy rainfall over the Aspen Acres burn scar is expected\nup to and during the period of the watch. Residents near the Aspen\nAcres burn scar should prepare for potential debris flow. Be sure\nto stay up to date with information from local authorities. Heavy\nrainfall could trigger flash flooding of low-lying areas, street\nflooding, and debris flows in and near recent wildfire burn scars.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- National Weather Service Meteorologists are forecasting heavy\nrainfall over the Aspen Acres burn scar, which may lead to flash\nflooding and debris flows.\n- Some locations that may experience flash flooding include...\nBeulah, San Isabel and Highways 165 and 78 in and around the\nAspen Acres Burn Scar.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-08-23T21:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Wet Mountains between 6300 and 10000Ft; Wet Mountains above 10000 Ft; Pueblo Vicinity/Pueblo County Below 6300 Feet","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.71c3db68638cddab763e762eca0867822f2c285c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.71c3db68638cddab763e762eca0867822f2c285c.001.1"},{"event":"Flash Flood Watch","headline":"Flash Flood Watch issued August 23 at 11:46AM MDT until August 24 at 9:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flash flooding and debris flows caused by excessive rainfall\ncontinue to be possible over the Aspen Acres burn scar.\n\n* WHERE...Aspen Acres Burn Scar.\n\n* WHEN...Until 9 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Heavy rainfall over the Aspen Acres burn scar is expected\nup to and during the period of the watch. Residents near the Aspen\nAcres burn scar should prepare for potential debris flow. Be sure\nto stay up to date with information from local authorities. Heavy\nrainfall could trigger flash flooding of low-lying areas, street\nflooding, and debris flows in and near recent wildfire burn scars.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- National Weather Service Meteorologists are forecasting heavy\nrainfall over the Aspen Acres burn scar, which may lead to flash\nflooding and debris flows.\n- Some locations that may experience flash flooding include...\nBeulah, San Isabel and Highways 165 and 78 in and around the\nAspen Acres Burn Scar.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-08-24T21:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Wet Mountains between 6300 and 10000Ft; Wet Mountains above 10000 Ft; Pueblo Vicinity/Pueblo County Below 6300 Feet","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.71c3db68638cddab763e762eca0867822f2c285c.001.2","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.71c3db68638cddab763e762eca0867822f2c285c.001.2"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-23T17:22:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 231722 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1122 AM MDT Sun Aug 23 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Increased flash flood potential over the Aspen Acres burn scar today, as showers and thunderstorms become more numerous across the area. - Showers and storms continue through much of the incoming week, though with a downtrend in coverage late week. && .SHORT TERM","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-23T17:23:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 231723 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1123 AM MDT Sun Aug 23 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-241730- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and 11000 Feet- Central Chaffee County